WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For those who don't know
your back story,

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were elected into Congress
in 2018.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:07.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're one of the first
two Muslim women in Congress

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.378 line:92%
-And first Palestinian-American.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-First Palestinian-America
woman.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-First Palestinian-America
woman.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:18.451
And what was it like entering --
How have you found it so far

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.386 line:92%
-I mean, it's interesting.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's kind of
a love/hate relationship.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.391
But my residents keep me
grounded and remind me every day

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
why I have to keep going there
and fighting for them.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.195 size:84% position:42%
So it's a very humbling
experience, as well.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.698
You should see some of the early
footage of me coming out.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.500
I was doing these selfies,
and I was super-excited.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Oh, my God.
I'm a congressmember."

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"How did this happen?"

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.341
You know, I didn't speak English
when I started school.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.175 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And my parents --

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mom only went up
to eighth-grade education.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.311 line:92%
My dad, fourth-grade education

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.781
And, you know, what's incredible
about this American story

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that they're a predominantl
non-Muslim community.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.386
Fellow Americans who didn'
share my faith or ethnicit

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.455
elected me,
and that's the part of the story

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wish people
would know more about.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:01:00.427
And I think it's just so much --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.761 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's so much light

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
during this really dark time
in our country right now.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were talking backstage
8 and 13, your boys?

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And how are they taking t

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
having a congresswoman
for a mother?

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's amazing. You should know
My son Adam is 13.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's --
He's like my policy adviser.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
He literally -- He watches
my committee hearings.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And, yeah, he goes,

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mom, how come you guys
didn't pass that amendment?"

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's crazy. And he
also goes, "How's Maxine?"

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Honey, that's
Chairwoman Waters to you."

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't -- I know. It's crazy.
But I love it.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.023 line:92%
And my 8-year-old, you know,

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love that I'm just Mom
when I get home.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.327
And, again, it just keeps me
humble, keeps me grounded.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.996
-So I want to talk about this.
We've had you booked for months.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:37.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've been very excited
about it.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were talking backstage.
You've had a crazy day.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You did a podcast.

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:43.303 size:78% position:39%
When did you actually
record the podcast?

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Last week.
-Okay, so, it came out.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:48.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of people
have been talking about it
both sides of the aisle.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were talking about
the tragedy of the Holocaust

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.114 line:92%
and you -- The words you use

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
was it gave you
a calming feeling

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you were happy
that it became a safe haven --

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:04.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
Palestine became a safe have
for the Jewish people.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:07.694 size:84% position:42%
Some criticized the use
of "calming feeling."

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have said
it was taken out of context.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.965
I want to give you a chanc
to provide some context.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and, you know,
for folks that don't know,

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.835 line:92%
I mean, my grandmother --

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:16.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
my living grandmother,
my mom's mom --

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:20.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
lives in the West Bank
in occupied territories
of Palestine.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.141 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And what's incredibly --

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
the tragedy of the Holocaust -

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, the reason
why Israel was created

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.981
was to create a safe haven
for Jews around the world.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:32.285 size:84% position:42%
And there is something,
in many ways, beautiful

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.220 line:92%
about that my ancestors --

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.488 line:92%
many had died or had to give u

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:36.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
their livelihood,
their human dignity

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.792 size:84% position:42%
to provide a safe haven
for Jews in our world.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.428 size:78% position:39%
And that is something
I wanted to recognize

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
and kind of honor
in some sort of way.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.965 line:92%
But I also think it's importan

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I want the Palestinian
people also to find

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.704
some sort of, you know, light in
this kind of what's happening.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.973 line:92%
But also, you know, in the end

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:57.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said I want all of us
to feel safe.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.012 line:92%
All of us deserve human dignity,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.281
no matter our backgrounds,
no matter our ethnicity,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter even our
political opinions.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:06.119 size:88% position:44%
We all deserve that kind
of equality and justice.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.387 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And, you know, for me,

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:10.023 size:88% position:44%
I wanted to uplift that
and bring that to light.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:10.857 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And it was unfortunate.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I got a text message
from a friend who's like,

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, next time,
you know, really clarify.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.130 line:92%
Maybe talk like a fourth grader.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.466
Because maybe the racist idiot
would understand you better.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:24.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's just -
You know, I will continue

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:25.338 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to speak truth to power

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
and continue to uplift
my grandmother through love.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's all I can do,
is continue to share

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
the human impact of
what it means to be Palestinia

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.380 line:92%
in the occupied territories.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I'm --
You know it's nice, I think,

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:39.385
to have someone in Congress as a
Palestinian who has a platform

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
because obviously it's never -
it happens very rarely.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.023
Certainly in the media you don't
get the Palestinian perspective.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:48.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
It does -- I actually thin
it wouldn't hurt for all of us

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:52.498
to talk about the history
of that part of the world

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:53.266 size:84% position:42% line:92%
on a fourth-grade level

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.069
because I actually don't think
a lot of us here understand it

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that there's -
A very, very bad-faith argumen

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:04.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
was made today that you were
calmed by the Holocaust.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.178 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Of course.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think there was
a good-faith argument

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe your history
did not --

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.818 size:75% position:38%
was not in alignment
with everyone else.

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:15.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, I mean, do you feel lik
there's a way to talk

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the history
of that part of the world

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.260
that people here in this country
that maybe

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't fully understand it
could grasp it more?

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
I mean, I think, for me,

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
I grew up in the most beautifu
blackest city in the world

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the country,
which is city of Detroit.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:31.204
And every corner is a reminder
of the Civil Rights Movement

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:34.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I, through my
African-American teachers --

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:37.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I call my black
mothers on the block

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.111 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I grew up in --

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:41.147
They, you know, constantly tol
me about the pain of oppression.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.683
They taught me
about the history of segregation

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
and feeling less than
and dehumanized

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they were black
in America.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.024
And a lot of that, that lens
that I bring to this issue -

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's how I talk about it
the fact that, you know,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:57.764
we are dehumanizing a whol
community to uplift others

00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:01.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I don't think that's truly
going to keep anybody safe

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.635 line:92%
It's truly not going to lead

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
towards peace and equality
and justice.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have to,
when you look at this issue,

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.907 line:92%
come from a place of values.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:10.076
You know, people want to g
ahead and jump and choose sides.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, come from a place of value
because, by the end,

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.982
you will choose the right side
of history when you do that.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:18.351 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned --
You mentioned your distric

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:22.088
and obviously the things -
You know, you're getting

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:24.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
attention today for sort o
international affairs.

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:26.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you also have to take care
of your district at home.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
Poverty's a very serious issue
at home.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.330
How are you addressing tha
back in Michigan's 13th?

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and the 13th
Congressional District

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.032 line:92%
knows I always have their back

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
They taught me to be
unapologetically, you know

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
myself in
speaking truth to power.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:39.539 size:75% position:38% line:92%
But they come first.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I have four
neighborhood service centers

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
where getting people through
everyday issues has to go

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:44.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
hand in hand
with the policy work.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:48.114
And, you know, the challenge
around economic oppression

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.615 line:92%
in many ways is something

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.284 size:81% position:41%
that they can't wait
for me to pass a bill.

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.720 size:78% position:39%
So I need to be able
to pick up the phone,

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.754 line:92%
use the power of the letterhead.

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:57.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, just the last --
A couple weeks ago,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.424 line:92%
a woman who's hearing-impaired

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
needed her Social Security
benefits,

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it took one phone call
for us to call,

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.930 size:84% position:42%
and we found out it was
an administrative error

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.432
on the part of the Social
Security Administration.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.067 line:92%
And we got her $38,000, Seth

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, to me, I was like,
"Oh. This is why I'm here.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to change people's live
today.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.774
They shouldn't wait years for us
to pass Medicare for all,

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:17.777
you know, minimum-wage increase,
and all the things that I thin

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:20.913
are critically important
in our country right now.

